---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Orientation page on opening a bank account. Facts verified 2026-07-28
// against the fetched official sources below. The headline finding: the conto
// di base is a statutory right tied to legal stay, not to registered residency.
const sources = [
  { title: "Normattiva — TUB (D.lgs 385/1993), art. 126-noviesdecies (diritto al conto di base)", url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:stato:decreto.legislativo:1993-09-01;385~art126noviesdecies!vig=' },
  { title: 'Normattiva — TUB, art. 126-vicies (apertura e motivi di rifiuto)', url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:stato:decreto.legislativo:1993-09-01;385~art126vicies!vig=' },
  { title: 'Normattiva — TUB, art. 126-viciessemel e 126-viciesbis (caratteristiche e spese)', url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:stato:decreto.legislativo:1993-09-01;385~art126viciessemel!vig=' },
  { title: 'Normattiva — TUB, artt. 126-quinquiesdecies e 126-septiesdecies (portabilità in 12 giorni, penale)', url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:stato:decreto.legislativo:1993-09-01;385~art126quinquiesdecies!vig=' },
  { title: 'Normattiva — DM MEF 3 maggio 2018, n. 70, artt. 4-5 (gratuità: ISEE 11.600 €, pensioni 18.000 €)', url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:ministero.economia.e.finanze:decreto:2018-05-03;70~art4!vig=' },
  { title: 'Normattiva — DPR 605/1973, artt. 6-7 (codice fiscale nei rapporti bancari)', url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:presidente.repubblica:decreto:1973-09-29;605~art7!vig=' },
  { title: 'Normattiva — D.L. 201/2011, art. 19 (imposta di bollo 34,20 €, esenzione sotto 5.000 € di giacenza media)', url: 'https://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:stato:decreto.legge:2011-12-06;201~art19!vig=' },
  { title: "Banca d'Italia — Il conto di base (economiapertutti)", url: 'https://economiapertutti.bancaditalia.it/aree-tematiche/conto-corrente/il-conto-di-base/index.html' },
  { title: "Banca d'Italia — Indagine sul costo dei conti correnti nel 2024", url: 'https://www.bancaditalia.it/pubblicazioni/indagine-costo-cc/indagine-costo-cc2025/index.html' },
  { title: 'Regolamento (UE) 260/2012, art. 9 (accessibilità dei pagamenti — nessuna discriminazione per IBAN)', url: 'http://web.archive.org/web/20260111052929/https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX%3A32012R0260' },
];
const costs = [
  ['Traditional bank account', '€101.10 / year average (2024)'],
  ['Online account', '€30.60 / year average'],
  ['Postal account', '€71.60 / year average'],
  ['Imposta di bollo (stamp duty)', '€34.20 / year — not due if your average annual balance stays at or below €5,000'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Opening a bank account in Italy"
  description="The conto di base is a legal right for anyone staying legally in the EU — no registered residency needed. Documents, the free tiers, refusal rules, real costs, and why your employer cannot demand an Italian IBAN."
  alternates={{ en: '/banking', it: '/it/banking' }}
  ogImage="/og/banking.png"
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Opening a bank account in Italy</h1>
    <p>
      Newcomers are often told they are stuck in a loop: no residency without an
      address, no account without residency. For one specific product that loop
      does not exist in law. Italy must offer a <strong>conto di base</strong> to
      any consumer <strong>staying legally in the EU</strong>, expressly
      "regardless of place of residence" (art. 126-noviesdecies TUB). Facts
      verified <time datetime="2026-07-28">28 July 2026</time>; orientation, not
      legal or financial advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Your legal right: the conto di base</h2>
    <p>
      Every bank, Poste Italiane and payment institution offering consumer
      accounts <strong>must</strong> offer this euro account. The entitlement
      covers anyone with a right to stay under EU or Italian law — the statute
      names <strong>people with no fixed abode and asylum seekers</strong>
      explicitly. It carries a single all-inclusive annual fee, and for the
      included operations no other charge may be added beyond taxes.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Included</strong>: incoming and outgoing bonifici, salary or pension crediting, a debit card for payments and ATM withdrawals, online banking at no extra cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Excluded by design</strong>: overdrafts and credit lines (legally prohibited on this account), a cheque book, a linked securities account.</li>
      <li><strong>One per person</strong>: it is for consumers only, and not available if you already hold another payment account in Italy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>When it is free</h2>
    <p>
      Two tiers cost nothing (DM 70/2018): if your <strong>ISEE is below
      €11,600</strong> the account is free <em>and</em> exempt from stamp duty;
      if you draw a <strong>pension of up to €18,000 gross a year</strong> the
      account is free but stamp duty still applies. Both need written
      self-certification, and the ISEE must be re-communicated to the bank
      <strong>by 31 May each year</strong> — miss it and the fee returns.
      Operations beyond the included package can still be charged in either tier.
    </p>

    <h2>What you need to bring</h2>
    <p>
      A <strong>valid identity document</strong> (anti-money-laundering rules;
      remote identification via SPID or CIE is also allowed) and your
      <a href="/eu-citizens/residency/codice-fiscale">codice fiscale</a>, which
      banks are required to record for anyone opening any relationship. If you
      are not yet resident and have no codice fiscale, the law lets the bank
      record your details with your foreign address instead — but get the codice
      fiscale first if you are actually moving: every bank will ask.
      No fetched official source makes a permesso di soggiorno a statutory
      precondition; the legal test is lawful stay. What individual banks accept
      as <em>evidence</em> of that varies, so ask before you queue.
    </p>

    <h2>If the bank says no</h2>
    <p>
      For the conto di base the grounds for refusal are a closed list: failing
      the legal requirements, already holding an Italian payment account, or
      anti-money-laundering concerns. A refusal must be given
      <strong>in writing, free of charge, within 10 working days</strong>, with
      the specific reasons and the routes to complain — a formal
      <em>reclamo</em>, an <em>esposto</em> to Banca d'Italia, or the banking
      ombudsman (<strong>ABF</strong>). Opening also cannot be made conditional
      on buying other products.
    </p>

    <h2>What accounts really cost</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full min-w-[480px] border-collapse text-sm">
      <tbody>
        {
          costs.map(([item, cost]) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">{item}</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 text-muted">{cost}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-6">
    <p>
      Those are Banca d'Italia's own survey figures for 2024 (weighted average
      across account types: €85.30). Compare the <em>Documento informativo sulle
      spese</em> and the total-cost indicator (ICC) before choosing — the
      regulator publishes both precisely so you can.
    </p>

    <h2>Keep your EU IBAN — or switch later</h2>
    <p>
      If you already bank elsewhere in the EU, you may not need an Italian
      account at all: under <strong>art. 9 of Regulation (EU) 260/2012</strong>
      a payee cannot require your account to be in a particular member state, so
      an Italian employer or utility <strong>must accept any SEPA-reachable EU
      IBAN</strong> for salary and direct debits. And if you do open one and
      regret it, switching is a consumer right: the new bank must move balance,
      standing orders and direct debits <strong>within 12 working days, free of
      charge</strong>, or owes you €40 plus a daily surcharge.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-line bg-white/60 p-6">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-xl">Sources</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      Primary, official sources this page is based on — each fetched and checked on 28 July 2026.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm">
      {
        sources.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <a href={s.url} class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">
              {s.title}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
